      "content": "that makes sense, but it feels like the \"accessible aesthetic language\" you mentioned is actually just a way to make political talking points more palatable. isn't there a risk that when art becomes too dependent on its political utility, it stops being \"art\" in the traditional sense and just becomes propaganda or social work?",
